1
00:04:04,444 --> 00:04:10,444
Gabriel's Redemption: Part I is a drama, romance film directed by Tosca Musk.

2
00:08:08,888 --> 00:08:14,888
After leaving his prestigious post at the University of Toronto, Gabriel embarks
on a new journey with Julia, and he is eager to become a father.

3
00:12:13,333 --> 00:12:19,333
However, Gabriel's idyllic vision is jeopardized when
Julia's intensive program becomes all consuming.

4
00:16:17,777 --> 00:16:23,777
When Julia is granted a prestigious opportunity to deliver an academic lecture at Oxford, Gabriel
challenges her about the subject of her presentation, which clashes with his own research.

5
00:20:22,222 --> 00:20:28,222
In Oxford, their past resurfaces, including an old nemesis determined to
humiliate Julia and expose one of Gabriel's well-guarded secrets.

6
00:24:26,666 --> 00:24:32,666
Emotions run high, alliances are tested, and the couple must confront the shadows of
their shared history in a battle for love, truth, and redemption.

7
00:28:31,111 --> 00:28:37,111
Gabriel, played by Giulio Berruti.

8
00:32:35,555 --> 00:32:41,555
Julia, played by Melanie Zanetti.

9
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Rachel, played by Julia Barrett-Mitchell.

10
00:40:44,444 --> 00:40:50,444
Christa, played by Margaux Brooke.

11
00:44:48,888 --> 00:44:54,888
Richard, played by Malachy Cleary.

12
00:48:53,333 --> 00:48:59,333
Tom, played by Kurt McKinney.

13
00:52:57,777 --> 00:53:03,777
Passionflix is an entertainment streaming platform and production company.

14
00:57:02,222 --> 00:57:08,222
Founded in 2017 by director and producer Tosca Musk, screenwriter Joany Kane, and producer Jina Panebianco, it focuses on
releasing original film adaptations of the best-selling romantic novels, while also streaming classic romantic movies.

15
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Passionflix also makes erotic thrillers.

16
01:05:11,111 --> 01:05:17,111
The Hollywood Reporter describes Passionflix productions in general as "saucier than Hallmark but much tamer
than porn, tamer even than some R-rated movies." No frontal nudity below the waist is shown.

17
01:09:15,555 --> 01:09:21,555
As co-founder and CEO Tosca Musk explains, "Passionflix is
there to remove shame from sexuality...

18
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
We are there to encourage connection, communication and compromise in relationships and we’re there to validate emotions." Movies and television series on this
platform are categorized according to a "barometer of naughtiness" ranging from "Oh so vanilla" (for romantic comedies) to "NSFW" (not safe for work).

19
01:17:24,444 --> 01:17:30,444
The New York Times characterizes these as having "simple"
plots and "sometimes unrefined" acting.

20
01:21:28,888 --> 01:21:34,888
Wired opines that the "acting is good, the actors are hot, and the plots deliver; don’t ask about the
cinematography." Each film has a budget of no more than $10 million and is typically shot within a fortnight.

21
01:25:33,333 --> 01:25:39,333
"Founding members" or "Signature members"—fans who paid a premium subscription—have the
right to be on set during filming and offer their views on what should be done.

22
01:29:37,777 --> 01:29:43,777
Some might even appear as extras.

23
01:33:42,222 --> 01:33:48,222
Musk likens this form of fan service to having her own "focus group" on set.

24
01:37:46,666 --> 01:37:52,666
Although the platform is technically available worldwide, licensed
contents can only be watched in the United States.

25
01:41:51,111 --> 01:41:57,111
Subtitles are available in nine languages.

26
01:45:55,555 --> 01:46:01,555
The tone is emotional.
